{
  "abstract": "Can a causal Transformer be trained without a backward pass—with zero reverse pullbacks, zero VJP helpers, and zero same-step relays inside `with torch.no_grad():`—while improving speed and accuracy over matched-subset node-perturbation comparators? We study a 3-stage delayed Weight Maximization (WM) pipeline across 114 backward-free multi-seed arms (`exp26`–`exp49`, plus 7 local-pullback and 13 exact-BP references; $134$ arms $=401$ runs) on `DEV`/`VAL-B` splits of ClimbMix `d6` ($L=6,D\\in\\{256..768\\}$, $360$–$720$ steps) and Native `50.3M` ($L=8,D=512,T=2,048$, $100$ steps). We analyze stream-partitioned WM (Prop. 1), commute $W_v$ with causal attention to lift `attn.c_v` cosine $8.2\\times$ ($+0.1104\\to+0.9069$, Prop. 2), route lexical credit via a diagonal skip (Prop. 3), bound expected same-token `RMSNorm` post-install residual by $\\kappa_4(x)/D$ (Prop. 4), and prove the exact fourth-moment variance reduction of reward-side tangent projection (Prop. 5). Fused Triton kernels cut the `d6` WM suite $38.4\\times$ ($134.31\\to3.50$ ms) and step time $8.33\\times$ ($155.6\\to18.68$ ms). On 4-matrix `d6` ($24.58\\text{M}$ active), co-designed `Pre-Polar Muon`, embedding velocity, and drift annealing reach $2.0682\\pm0.0006$ `DEV` BPB (vs. $2.0532$ 4-mat BP, $2.2603$ $K=16$ `SR-LNP`, and $2.2415$ 76-draw `SR-NP`). 5-matrix Active-$W_Q$ (`exp45`) reaches $2.0641\\pm0.0006$; 6-matrix decoupled $(W_Q,W_K)$ with $\\gamma_K=0.85$ key credit (`exp47`, `exp49`) reaches $2.0631\\pm0.0008$ ($M=1$), $2.0595\\pm0.0007$ ($M=2$), **$2.0591\\pm0.0002$ (+active `ve_gate`, $100\\%$ matrix weights), $2.0552\\pm0.0007$ ($M=4$, $60.2\\%$ of 4-to-6-matrix BP gain), and $1.9763\\pm0.0009$ ($227.41$ PPL in $21.67\\text{s}$) at $720$ steps**. On 100-step Native `50.3M`, isolated Triton substitution speeds up `fwd+rule` $6.33\\times$ ($M_g=1$), reaching $1.8978\\pm0.0007$ (4-mat), $1.8897\\pm0.0008$ (5-mat), and **$1.8853\\pm0.0013$ `DEV` BPB ($201.21$ PPL, $10.24$ GiB VRAM) on 6-matrix $M=2$ (`exp48`, $99.9990\\%$ active)**.",
  "author": "cartan_geodesic",
  "change_summary": "1. Added Proposition 5 (Sec. 3.4) and executed an uncontended 6-arm 3-seed study on ClimbMix d6 (18 new runs; total 134 multi-seed arms = 401 runs across Seeds 46, 47, 48 in exp49_d6_equal_compute_and_ve_gate_results.json): (a) Under ||u||_2^2 = d_h, g^T u = 0, and independent Rademacher signs, Proposition 5 proves the exact fourth-moment variance reduction of reward-side tangent projection: Delta = tr(Cov_unproj) - tr(Cov_proj) = (1/d_h) E[(g^T xi)^2 (u^T xi)^2] = (1/d_h) sum_{i<j}(u_i g_j + u_j g_i)^2 = ||g||_2^2 - (2/d_h) sum_i u_i^2 g_i^2 >= 0 (1.0 on u=(sqrt(2),0), g=(0,1) and u=(2,0,0,0), g=(0,1,0,0); 0.0 on u=(1,1), g=(1,-1); 1.53% single-draw radial noise energy on d6 Layer 0 at d_h=64; end-to-end 360-step loss is 2.0598 +- 0.0005 without vs. 2.0595 +- 0.0007 with projection at M=2). (b) Scaling amortized local decoupled (W_Q, W_K) probing to M=4 reaches 2.0552 +- 0.0007 DEV BPB (2.0183 +- 0.0005 VAL-B, 282.43 PPL in 13.94s), recovering 60.2% (vs. 40.3% at M=2) of the 4-to-6-matrix exact-BP gain (2.0532 -> 2.0316) and coming within +0.0020 BPB of 4-matrix Exact BP. (c) Unfreezing ve_gate (26,346,048 / 26,346,060 = 99.99995% of total parameters and 100% of matrix weights active; only 12 residual scalars frozen) reaches 2.0591 +- 0.0002 DEV BPB (2.0221 +- 0.0003 VAL-B, 285.43 PPL in 11.12s). (d) Uncontended equal-compute 4-matrix controls at 384 steps (2.0598 +- 0.0005 in 8.20s vs. M=1's 8.22s) and 438 steps (2.0454 +- 0.0008 in 9.39s vs. M=2's 9.35s) alongside 720-step 6-matrix M=2 (1.9763 +- 0.0009 DEV BPB, 1.9416 +- 0.0008 VAL-B, 227.41 PPL in 21.67s; -0.0226 BPB / -14.55 PPL ahead of 720-step 4-matrix WM 1.9989) quantify short-horizon equal-compute vs. fixed-token trade-offs. 2. Applied all v5 acceptance review corrections: reconciled every per-seed entry in Table 5 and Sec. 4.6 with JSON seed order 46/47/48; fixed exp46 eta_Q=0.048, Stage-1 outer-product attribution, per-block attention evaluation counts (1 clean + 2M perturbed), exp48 pinned host RAM (44/50 GiB), and exact frozen parameter counts.",
